      <uei>uei.opennms.org/vendor/RANSecure/traps/rsBroadcastStorm</uei>
      <event-label>RAN-SECURE-NET-SIM-MIB defined trap event: rsBroadcastStorm</event-label>
      <descr>&lt;p&gt;Broadcast storm on port &lt;b&gt;%parm[#1]%&lt;/b&gt; of %nodelabel% (%parm[#2]%): &lt;b&gt;%parm[#3]% broadcast packets per second&lt;/b&gt;, above the storm-control threshold.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;The usual cause is a layer-2 loop at the customer site (a cable plugged twice into the customer's own switch). The storm consumes switch CPU and bandwidth and can affect other customers in the same VLAN.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Recommended action: confirm storm-control is shutting or rate-limiting the port, contact the customer to remove the loop, and verify STP is enabled on the customer-facing port.&lt;/p&gt;</descr>
      <logmsg dest="logndisplay">&lt;p&gt;Broadcast storm on %parm[#1]% (%parm[#2]%): %parm[#3]% pps.&lt;/p&gt;</logmsg>
      <severity>Major</severity>
      <alarm-data reduction-key="%uei%:%dpname%:%nodeid%:%parm[#1]%" alarm-type="1" auto-clean="false"/>
   </event>
